[2026-09-21 15:19:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 150]   step_150_channel_dissociation — reconstruction-error sensitivity audit of
[2026-09-21 15:19:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 150]   the two post-2017 transit channels.
[2026-09-21 15:19:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 150]   The post-2017 cohort dissociates the transit instrument's two channels on
[2026-09-21 15:19:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 150]   the SAME members: the reconstruction-dependent periapsis-rotation channel
[2026-09-21 15:19:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 150]   fails to transfer the declared-axis contrast (step_117: perm p = 0.92, sign
[2026-09-21 15:19:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 150]   reversed) and its catalogue-discrepancy residual field attenuates in the
[2026-09-21 15:19:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 150]   densest-observation stratum (step_118 T12: gap +0.10 to +0.20 dex on the
[2026-09-21 15:19:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 150]   moderate-quality strata, -0.02 dex at n_obs > 1000), while the
[2026-09-21 15:19:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 150]   reconstruction-insensitive aphelion-dipole channel replicates the declared
[2026-09-21 15:19:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 150]   axis on the identical cohort (step_124: d_par = +0.095, tide-aware
[2026-09-21 15:19:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 150]   p = 0.0021) flat across the same quality strata (+0.091 / +0.098 / +0.093
[2026-09-21 15:19:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 150]   dex).
[2026-09-21 15:19:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 150]   This step tests the mechanistic premise of that dissociation: that
[2026-09-21 15:19:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 150]   realistic short-arc orbit-solution errors move the leg-to-leg boundary
[2026-09-21 15:19:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 150]   rotation strongly but move the aphelion direction negligibly.  If the
[2026-09-21 15:19:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 150]   rotation channel is orders of magnitude more sensitive to the element
[2026-09-21 15:19:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 150]   errors that short-arc fits inflate, the observed dissociation is the
[2026-09-21 15:19:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 150]   predicted signature of a reconstruction systematic — it can only enter
[2026-09-21 15:19:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 150]   the channel that passes through an orbit solution at leg resolution.
[2026-09-21 15:19:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 150]   Method: for each comet of a quality-stratified post-2017 sample, inject
[2026-09-21 15:19:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 150]   Monte-Carlo perturbations of the fitted elements drawn from the object's
[2026-09-21 15:19:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 150]   own SBDB element sigmas (data/raw/mpc/sbdb_fp/), rebuild the osculating
[2026-09-21 15:19:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 150]   state, and propagate BOTH legs to the +/-250 AU barycentric sphere with
[2026-09-21 15:19:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 150]   the identical REBOUND/IAS15 + DE440s machinery the boundary record uses
[2026-09-21 15:19:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 150]   (scripts/utils/lpc_boundary.integrate_leg).  Per draw the displacement of
[2026-09-21 15:19:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 150]   the rotation observable (drot = sep(inbound, outbound asymptote)) and of
[2026-09-21 15:19:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 150]   the aphelion observable (aph = -inbound asymptote) is recorded.
[2026-09-21 15:19:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 150]   T1  per-comet sensitivity: RMS sigma_drot vs sigma_aph per object; the
[2026-09-21 15:19:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 150]   median and distribution of the ratio sigma_drot / sigma_aph.
[2026-09-21 15:19:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 150]   T2  element-group attribution: perturbations restricted to the
[2026-09-21 15:19:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 150]   weakly-constrained (short-arc-dominated) directions tp, e, q versus
[2026-09-21 15:19:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 150]   the angular directions om, i, w — which error budget drives each
[2026-09-21 15:19:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 150]   channel.
[2026-09-21 15:19:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 150]   T3  quality gradient: Spearman of sigma_drot and of sigma_aph against
[2026-09-21 15:19:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 150]   n_obs and data_arc — the predicted noise stratification, compared to
[2026-09-21 15:19:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 150]   the OBSERVED stratification of the residual field (b82 T12) and of
[2026-09-21 15:19:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 150]   the aphelion lean (b88 T3).
[2026-09-21 15:19:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 150]   T4  matched-error-scale: the aphelion displacement at the perturbation
[2026-09-21 15:19:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 150]   scale that reproduces the observed short-arc rotation-residual
[2026-09-21 15:19:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 150]   inflation (gap ~0.27 dex, i.e. drot inflated ~1.9x).
